@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-refusals`
IMPORT `nii-il04-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il04-published-figures`
IMPORT `nii-s1-definitions`
IMPORT `nii-s334-interpretation`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-j-tables`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-j`
IMPORT `nii-s337-rates`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-04: National Insurance Law s 334, Schedule J.
--
-- Imports this row's nouns and refusals and IL-04's modules, and no other row.
-- Exposes the reduced collection threshold and this row's record of Schedule J
-- column D amounts on a wage, one per branch, which the IL-05 adapter hands to
-- IL-05's s 342(c). Both rows declare `A branch of insurance` (RECONCILE.md,
-- clash N1); here the constructors are IL-04's.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-04`

§§ `Section 334(a) — the reduced collection threshold`

-- 2026: 7,703, the Institute's published figure (IL-04 NOTES.md assumption A4).
-- Any other year: IL-04's own refusal.
@ref NII s 334(a) (row IL-04, nii-s334-interpretation.l4)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-04: the reduced collection threshold for a month in` `the year` MEANS
    `s 334(a) — the reduced collection threshold for a month in` `the year`

§§ `Schedule J, column D — the deduction from the employee's wage, per branch`

-- IL-04's column D rule takes "the average wage" because the 2025 text of
-- Schedule J began column D's upper part at 60% of it. Every version IL-04
-- reads for 2026 on begins it at the reduced collection threshold (IL-04 fork
-- F3, repaired 2026-10-07), so the figure is never read; IL-04 leaves open which
-- average wage it would be (its fork F5). The capstone passes no figure: a named
-- refusal, reached only if some version did read it.
@ref NII Schedule J column D (row IL-04, nii-schedule-j.l4; IL-04 forks F3, F5)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-07 passes no average wage to Schedule J column D, which IL-04 reads for 2026 on without one` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-07 passes no average wage to Schedule J column D, which IL-04 reads for 2026 on without one"

@ref NII Schedule J column D (row IL-04, nii-schedule-j.l4)
GIVEN `the year`   IS A NUMBER
      `the wage`   IS A NUMBER
      `the branch` IS A `A branch of insurance`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-04: the column D amount in a month of` `the year` `on a wage of` `the wage` `in the branch of` `the branch` MEANS
    `the column D deduction under` (`Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` `the year`)
        `on a wage of` `the wage`
        `with the threshold at` (`s 334(a) — the reduced collection threshold for a month in` `the year`)
        `and the average wage at` `IL-07 passes no average wage to Schedule J column D, which IL-04 reads for 2026 on without one`
        `in the branches` (LIST `the branch`)

-- The six branches Schedule J's column D prints a figure for (IL-04's tests check
-- it; they are also the branches s 342(c)(1) names, row IL-05 fork F12).
@ref NII Schedule J column D (row IL-04, nii-schedule-j.l4)
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the wage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `IL-07 column D amounts on the earner's wage`
`IL-04: the column D amounts in a month of` `the year` `on a wage of` `the wage` MEANS
    `IL-07 column D amounts on the earner's wage` WITH
        `the column D amount for maternity`                     IS `on` `maternity`
        `the column D amount for accident injury`               IS `on` `accident injury`
        `the column D amount for unemployment`                  IS `on` `unemployment`
        `the column D amount for disability`                    IS `on` `disability`
        `the column D amount for long-term care`                IS `on` `long-term care`
        `the column D amount for senior citizens and survivors` IS `on` `senior citizens and survivors`
    WHERE
        `on` b MEANS `IL-04: the column D amount in a month of` `the year` `on a wage of` `the wage` `in the branch of` b

§§ `Schedule J, for the tests`

-- The percentage column D prints for a branch on each part of the wage, in the
-- version for a month of the year. Used by the tests to show the figures the
-- hand arithmetic in NOTES.md reads.
@ref NII Schedule J column D (row IL-04, nii-schedule-j.l4)
GIVEN `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      `the upper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-04: column D's combined percentage in the deduction branches, in a month of` `the year` `, on the upper part:` `the upper` MEANS
    sum (map `the figure for` (LIST `maternity`, `accident injury`, `unemployment`, `disability`, `long-term care`, `senior citizens and survivors`))
    WHERE
        v MEANS `Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` `the year`
        `the column` MEANS
            IF `the upper` THEN `column D, upper part of the wage` ELSE `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold`
        `the figure for` b MEANS `the percentage in column D of` v `for` b `in` `the column`

-- The printed totals row, column D, for the version of a month of the year: the
-- figure the Institute's published composite matches (IL-04 fork F4).
@ref NII Schedule J totals row (row IL-04, nii-schedule-j.l4; IL-04 fork F4)
GIVEN `the year`  IS A NUMBER
      `the upper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-04: column D's printed total, in a month of` `the year` `, on the upper part:` `the upper` MEANS
    `the printed total of` ((`Schedule J — the version for a contribution month in` `the year`)'s `totals`) `in` `the column`
    WHERE
        `the column` MEANS
            IF `the upper` THEN `column D, upper part of the wage` ELSE `column D, part of the wage not above the threshold`
